  "servings": 4,
  "summary": "This <b>classic French beef braise</b> delivers deep, luxurious flavor in a fraction of the traditional cooking time by using pressure techniques tailored for busy weekday evenings. Bone-in short ribs are seasoned and quickly seared to develop a rich, dark crust, locking in savory juices before entering the pot. Whole golden shallots, sliced fresh carrots, and smashed garlic cloves form a fragrant aromatics base that caramelizes lightly in the rendered pan drippings. A full-bodied red wine reduction dissolves all the caramelized bits from the bottom of the pot, creating an intensely savory liquid base enriched with rich beef broth and sprigs of earthy garden thyme. As the stew cooks under pressure, the connective tissues melt into tender perfection while the red wine sauce reduces to a silky finish. A final touch of cold butter stirred in right before serving gives the glossy sauce a velvety texture that coats every bite of tender beef. Pair this comforting dish with creamy mashed potatoes, crusty sourdough bread, or buttered egg noodles to catch every drop of the savory gravy.",
